cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "explore_unios: a prerequisite-graph course scheduler and an MCP server for the SUJJS (Osijek) course catalog"
message: "If you use this software or its data extraction approach, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pitlović
    given-names: Fabijan
    # email / affiliation / ORCID: add when finalizing
  - family-names: Mostarkić
    given-names: Fran
repository-code: "https://github.com/pitfa19/explore_unizg"
url: "https://explore-unios.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Two tools for planning studies at Sveučilište Josipa Jurja Strossmayera u Osijeku (SUJJS). A
  browser app models a study programme as a prerequisite DAG and computes the earliest possible
  completion, respecting both prerequisite depth and the winter/summer season a course is taught
  in. An MCP server and Agent Skill give a language model read-only access to the ISVU public
  course catalog, covering all 18 SUJJS constituents and roughly 9,500 courses, and can export a
  programme in the scheduler's import format.
keywords:
  - University of Osijek
  - SUJJS
  - ISVU
  - course catalog
  - curriculum
  - prerequisite graph
  - directed acyclic graph
  - study planning
  - Model Context Protocol
